The course at a glance. Sessions 1-2 refresh the mathematics and programming the rest of the course uses. Sessions 3-6 cover classical bioinformatics: databases, alignment, database searches with profiles, and protein structure. In Sessions 7-9 the two subjects meet: a profile score turns out to be a simple neural network, and the networks are trained properly. Sessions 10-12 cover modern deep learning, up to AlphaFold. One problem, predicting protein structure from sequence, runs through the second half and ends in your capstone project.




